#: ../../../../Users/chang137/Documents/kaiwu_torch_plugin_docs/docs/source/getting_started/tutorials/quantum_sampling_bottleneck.md:1
msgid "Why Quantum? Revisiting the Sampling Bottleneck"
msgstr "Why Quantum? Revisiting the Sampling Bottleneck"

#: ../../../../Users/chang137/Documents/kaiwu_torch_plugin_docs/docs/source/getting_started/tutorials/quantum_sampling_bottleneck.md:3
msgid ""
"By this point you have finished the [Getting Started](../index.md) guide and"
" reviewed the [Prerequisites](../background.md). The [Theoretical "
"Foundations](../../theoretical-foundations/index.md) established that "
"Boltzmann machines are conceptually elegant but computationally crippled by "
"the **sampling bottleneck**. This chapter recaps that conclusion, explains "
"what quantum hardware changes, and shows how KPP lets you use classical and "
"Coherent Ising Machine (CIM) samplers through the same training workflow. It"
" is a bridge: the full derivations live in Theoretical Foundations, and the "
"code lives in the next two chapters."
msgstr ""
"By this point you have finished the [Getting Started](../index.md) guide and"
" reviewed the [Prerequisites](../background.md). The [Theoretical "
"Foundations](../../theoretical-foundations/index.md) established that "
"Boltzmann machines are conceptually elegant but computationally crippled by "
"the **sampling bottleneck**. This chapter recaps that conclusion, explains "
"what quantum hardware changes, and shows how KPP lets you use classical and "
"Coherent Ising Machine (CIM) samplers through the same training workflow. It"
" is a bridge: the full derivations live in Theoretical Foundations, and the "
"code lives in the next two chapters."

#: ../../../../Users/chang137/Documents/kaiwu_torch_plugin_docs/docs/source/getting_started/tutorials/quantum_sampling_bottleneck.md:5
msgid "The Sampling Problem in Exact Maximum Likelihood Learning"
msgstr "The Sampling Problem in Exact Maximum Likelihood Learning"

#: ../../../../Users/chang137/Documents/kaiwu_torch_plugin_docs/docs/source/getting_started/tutorials/quantum_sampling_bottleneck.md:9
msgid ""
"\\frac{\\partial \\mathcal{L}}{\\partial \\theta} =\n"
"\\mathbb{E}_{\\mathrm{data}}\\!\\left[ \\frac{\\partial E_\\theta}{\\partial \\theta} \\right] -\n"
"\\mathbb{E}_{\\mathrm{model}}\\!\\left[ \\frac{\\partial E_\\theta}{\\partial \\theta} \\right]."
msgstr ""
"\\frac{\\partial \\mathcal{L}}{\\partial \\theta} =\n"
"\\mathbb{E}_{\\mathrm{data}}\\!\\left[ \\frac{\\partial E_\\theta}{\\partial \\theta} \\right] -\n"
"\\mathbb{E}_{\\mathrm{model}}\\!\\left[ \\frac{\\partial E_\\theta}{\\partial \\theta} \\right]."

#: ../../../../Users/chang137/Documents/kaiwu_torch_plugin_docs/docs/source/getting_started/tutorials/quantum_sampling_bottleneck.md:18
msgid ""
"Classical approaches have known drawbacks (detailed in [Section "
"4.1](../../theoretical-foundations/kpp-theoretical-foundations-bm-"
"overall.md), [Section 4.2](../../theoretical-foundations/kpp-theoretical-"
"foundations-bm-restricted.md), and [Section 3.3](../../theoretical-"
"foundations/kpp-theoretical-foundations-ebms-cd.md)):"
msgstr ""
"Classical approaches have known drawbacks (detailed in [Section "
"4.1](../../theoretical-foundations/kpp-theoretical-foundations-bm-"
"overall.md), [Section 4.2](../../theoretical-foundations/kpp-theoretical-"
"foundations-bm-restricted.md), and [Section 3.3](../../theoretical-"
"foundations/kpp-theoretical-foundations-ebms-cd.md)):"

#: ../../../../Users/chang137/Documents/kaiwu_torch_plugin_docs/docs/source/getting_started/tutorials/quantum_sampling_bottleneck.md:20
msgid ""
"**MCMC / Gibbs sampling** converges to the target distribution, but mixing "
"can be exponentially slow in rugged energy landscapes — *critical slowing "
"down*."
msgstr ""
"**MCMC / Gibbs sampling** converges to the target distribution, but mixing "
"can be exponentially slow in rugged energy landscapes — *critical slowing "
"down*."

#: ../../../../Users/chang137/Documents/kaiwu_torch_plugin_docs/docs/source/getting_started/tutorials/quantum_sampling_bottleneck.md:21
msgid ""
"**CD / PCD** trade bias for speed: a few MCMC steps initialized at data "
"points, risking **mode collapse**; PCD keeps persistent chains but still "
"pays a sampling cost per update."
msgstr ""
"**CD / PCD** trade bias for speed: a few MCMC steps initialized at data "
"points, risking **mode collapse**; PCD keeps persistent chains but still "
"pays a sampling cost per update."

#: ../../../../Users/chang137/Documents/kaiwu_torch_plugin_docs/docs/source/getting_started/tutorials/quantum_sampling_bottleneck.md:23
msgid ""
"These methods are practical, but they should not be confused with exact "
"sampling from the equilibrium distribution."
msgstr ""
"These methods are practical, but they should not be confused with exact "
"sampling from the equilibrium distribution."

#: ../../../../Users/chang137/Documents/kaiwu_torch_plugin_docs/docs/source/getting_started/tutorials/quantum_sampling_bottleneck.md:25
msgid "The Quantum Alternative: Sampling by Physical Evolution"
msgstr "The Quantum Alternative: Sampling by Physical Evolution"

#: ../../../../Users/chang137/Documents/kaiwu_torch_plugin_docs/docs/source/getting_started/tutorials/quantum_sampling_bottleneck.md:27
msgid ""
"Instead of simulating a Markov chain, the energy function is encoded into a "
"physical quantum system that evolves toward its low-energy states. Devices "
"such as quantum annealers and Coherent Ising Machines (CIMs) realize this: "
"model variables are mapped to qubits or optical pulses, and measurements "
"yield samples from a distribution approximating the Boltzmann distribution "
"at the hardware's effective temperature:"
msgstr ""
"Instead of simulating a Markov chain, the energy function is encoded into a "
"physical quantum system that evolves toward its low-energy states. Devices "
"such as quantum annealers and Coherent Ising Machines (CIMs) realize this: "
"model variables are mapped to qubits or optical pulses, and measurements "
"yield samples from a distribution approximating the Boltzmann distribution "
"at the hardware's effective temperature:"

#: ../../../../Users/chang137/Documents/kaiwu_torch_plugin_docs/docs/source/getting_started/tutorials/quantum_sampling_bottleneck.md:29
msgid "P(\\mathbf{s}) \\propto \\exp\\left(-\\beta_{\\mathrm{eff}} H(\\mathbf{s})\\right),"
msgstr "P(\\mathbf{s}) \\propto \\exp\\left(-\\beta_{\\mathrm{eff}} H(\\mathbf{s})\\right),"

#: ../../../../Users/chang137/Documents/kaiwu_torch_plugin_docs/docs/source/getting_started/tutorials/quantum_sampling_bottleneck.md:36
msgid "The main promises are:"
msgstr "The main promises are:"

#: ../../../../Users/chang137/Documents/kaiwu_torch_plugin_docs/docs/source/getting_started/tutorials/quantum_sampling_bottleneck.md:38
msgid ""
"**Direct physical sampling**: quantum tunneling may escape local minima more"
" efficiently than thermal hopping."
msgstr ""
"**Direct physical sampling**: quantum tunneling may escape local minima more"
" efficiently than thermal hopping."

#: ../../../../Users/chang137/Documents/kaiwu_torch_plugin_docs/docs/source/getting_started/tutorials/quantum_sampling_bottleneck.md:39
msgid ""
"**Inherent parallelism**: thousands of optical pulses interact "
"simultaneously, versus sequential Gibbs updates."
msgstr ""
"**Inherent parallelism**: thousands of optical pulses interact "
"simultaneously, versus sequential Gibbs updates."

#: ../../../../Users/chang137/Documents/kaiwu_torch_plugin_docs/docs/source/getting_started/tutorials/quantum_sampling_bottleneck.md:40
msgid ""
"**Hardware-scale sampling**: problem sizes that would be prohibitively slow "
"to simulate classically."
msgstr ""
"**Hardware-scale sampling**: problem sizes that would be prohibitively slow "
"to simulate classically."

#: ../../../../Users/chang137/Documents/kaiwu_torch_plugin_docs/docs/source/getting_started/tutorials/quantum_sampling_bottleneck.md:41
msgid ""
"**Avoiding CD bias**: near-equilibrium samples without data-dependent "
"initialization, giving less biased gradient estimates."
msgstr ""
"**Avoiding CD bias**: near-equilibrium samples without data-dependent "
"initialization, giving less biased gradient estimates."

#: ../../../../Users/chang137/Documents/kaiwu_torch_plugin_docs/docs/source/getting_started/tutorials/quantum_sampling_bottleneck.md:43
msgid "From Boltzmann Machines to Ising Hamiltonians"
msgstr "From Boltzmann Machines to Ising Hamiltonians"

#: ../../../../Users/chang137/Documents/kaiwu_torch_plugin_docs/docs/source/getting_started/tutorials/quantum_sampling_bottleneck.md:47
msgid ""
"H(\\mathbf{s}) = -\\sum_i h_i s_i - \\sum_{i<j} J_{ij} s_i s_j + "
"\\mathrm{const},"
msgstr ""
"H(\\mathbf{s}) = -\\sum_i h_i s_i - \\sum_{i<j} J_{ij} s_i s_j + "
"\\mathrm{const},"

#: ../../../../Users/chang137/Documents/kaiwu_torch_plugin_docs/docs/source/getting_started/tutorials/quantum_sampling_bottleneck.md:52
msgid ""
"the form that quantum annealing hardware and CIMs are designed to handle. "
"KPP constructs this Ising matrix from the model parameters and hands it to "
"the **Kaiwu SDK solver**; you never need to perform the conversion by hand."
msgstr ""
"the form that quantum annealing hardware and CIMs are designed to handle. "
"KPP constructs this Ising matrix from the model parameters and hands it to "
"the **Kaiwu SDK solver**; you never need to perform the conversion by hand."

#: ../../../../Users/chang137/Documents/kaiwu_torch_plugin_docs/docs/source/getting_started/tutorials/quantum_sampling_bottleneck.md:54
msgid "Classical and Quantum Samplers in KPP"
msgstr "Classical and Quantum Samplers in KPP"

#: ../../../../Users/chang137/Documents/kaiwu_torch_plugin_docs/docs/source/getting_started/tutorials/quantum_sampling_bottleneck.md:56
msgid ""
"KPP uses different sampling backends through the same `sample(sampler)` "
"call, used in the [Quick Start](../quickstart.md) example. "
"`SimulatedAnnealingOptimizer` suits local debugging and baseline "
"experiments; `CIMOptimizer` requires valid Kaiwu SDK credentials and real-"
"machine access. The two should be compared on the same model, sampling "
"budget, and evaluation metrics, never inferred from the sampler type alone."
msgstr ""
"KPP uses different sampling backends through the same `sample(sampler)` "
"call, used in the [Quick Start](../quickstart.md) example. "
"`SimulatedAnnealingOptimizer` suits local debugging and baseline "
"experiments; `CIMOptimizer` requires valid Kaiwu SDK credentials and real-"
"machine access. The two should be compared on the same model, sampling "
"budget, and evaluation metrics, never inferred from the sampler type alone."

#: ../../../../Users/chang137/Documents/kaiwu_torch_plugin_docs/docs/source/getting_started/tutorials/quantum_sampling_bottleneck.md:66
msgid "Summary"
msgstr "Summary"

#: ../../../../Users/chang137/Documents/kaiwu_torch_plugin_docs/docs/source/getting_started/tutorials/quantum_sampling_bottleneck.md:68
msgid ""
"Sampling from the model distribution is the central computational bottleneck"
" of Boltzmann machine training (Eq. {eq}`eq-nll-gradient`)."
msgstr ""
"Sampling from the model distribution is the central computational bottleneck"
" of Boltzmann machine training (Eq. {eq}`eq-nll-gradient`)."

#: ../../../../Users/chang137/Documents/kaiwu_torch_plugin_docs/docs/source/getting_started/tutorials/quantum_sampling_bottleneck.md:69
msgid ""
"Classical MCMC suffers from slow mixing times, and practical approximations "
"such as CD introduce bias and can cause mode collapse."
msgstr ""
"Classical MCMC suffers from slow mixing times, and practical approximations "
"such as CD introduce bias and can cause mode collapse."

#: ../../../../Users/chang137/Documents/kaiwu_torch_plugin_docs/docs/source/getting_started/tutorials/quantum_sampling_bottleneck.md:70
msgid ""
"Quantum sampling encodes the energy as an Ising Hamiltonian and samples by "
"physical evolution, promising better mixing, parallelism, and less bias."
msgstr ""
"Quantum sampling encodes the energy as an Ising Hamiltonian and samples by "
"physical evolution, promising better mixing, parallelism, and less bias."

#: ../../../../Users/chang137/Documents/kaiwu_torch_plugin_docs/docs/source/getting_started/tutorials/quantum_sampling_bottleneck.md:71
msgid ""
"KPP converts model parameters into an Ising problem and connects classical "
"and quantum backends through a unified sampling interface."
msgstr ""
"KPP converts model parameters into an Ising problem and connects classical "
"and quantum backends through a unified sampling interface."

#: ../../../../Users/chang137/Documents/kaiwu_torch_plugin_docs/docs/source/getting_started/tutorials/quantum_sampling_bottleneck.md:72
msgid ""
"The next chapter establishes the classical baseline, [Simulated Annealing "
"for Ising Models](simulated_annealing.md), before the quantum integration in"
" [Integrating Quantum Samplers into PyTorch](quantum_sampling_pytorch.md)."
msgstr ""
"The next chapter establishes the classical baseline, [Simulated Annealing "
"for Ising Models](simulated_annealing.md), before the quantum integration in"
" [Integrating Quantum Samplers into PyTorch](quantum_sampling_pytorch.md)."

msgid ""
"Recall from [Section 3.1, Defining the Objective: Low Energy for Real "
"Data](../../theoretical-foundations/kpp-theoretical-foundations-ebms-def.md)"
" that the gradient of the negative log-likelihood for an energy-based model "
"decomposes into two expectations (Eq. {eq}`eq-nll-gradient-tf` in "
"Theoretical Foundations):"
msgstr ""
"Recall from [Section 3.1, Defining the Objective: Low Energy for Real "
"Data](../../theoretical-foundations/kpp-theoretical-foundations-ebms-def.md)"
" that the gradient of the negative log-likelihood for an energy-based model "
"decomposes into two expectations (Eq. {eq}`eq-nll-gradient-tf` in "
"Theoretical Foundations):"

msgid ""
"The data term is approximated by averaging over mini-batches. The model term"
" requires sampling from the current Boltzmann distribution, and computing it"
" exactly is #P-hard because it needs the partition function (Eq. {eq}`eq-"
"partition`; [Section 3.2, The Intractable Partition Function "
"Problem](../../theoretical-foundations/kpp-theoretical-foundations-ebms-"
"partition.md)). We must therefore sample, and training quality hinges on how"
" close the samples are to the target distribution, and how much they cost."
msgstr ""
"The data term is approximated by averaging over mini-batches. The model term"
" requires sampling from the current Boltzmann distribution, and computing it"
" exactly is #P-hard because it needs the partition function (Eq. {eq}`eq-"
"partition`; [Section 3.2, The Intractable Partition Function "
"Problem](../../theoretical-foundations/kpp-theoretical-foundations-ebms-"
"partition.md)). We must therefore sample, and training quality hinges on how"
" close the samples are to the target distribution, and how much they cost."

msgid ""
"where $\\beta_{\\mathrm{eff}}$ is the effective inverse temperature "
"([Section 1.2, The Boltzmann Distribution and "
"Equilibrium](../../theoretical-foundations/kpp-theoretical-foundations-stat-"
"boltzmann.md), Eq. {eq}`eq-boltzmann-dist`)."
msgstr ""
"where $\\beta_{\\mathrm{eff}}$ is the effective inverse temperature "
"([Section 1.2, The Boltzmann Distribution and "
"Equilibrium](../../theoretical-foundations/kpp-theoretical-foundations-stat-"
"boltzmann.md), Eq. {eq}`eq-boltzmann-dist`)."

msgid ""
"The mapping follows directly from the spin-glass analogy ([Section 1.1, The "
"Relationship Between Statistical Physics and Neural "
"Networks](../../theoretical-foundations/kpp-theoretical-foundations-stat-"
"spinglass.md); Eq. {eq}`eq-ising-hamiltonian`): binary variables $x_i \\in "
"\\{0, 1\\}$ become Ising spins $s_i = 2x_i - 1$, turning the quadratic "
"energy into an Ising Hamiltonian:"
msgstr ""
"The mapping follows directly from the spin-glass analogy ([Section 1.1, The "
"Relationship Between Statistical Physics and Neural "
"Networks](../../theoretical-foundations/kpp-theoretical-foundations-stat-"
"spinglass.md); Eq. {eq}`eq-ising-hamiltonian`): binary variables $x_i \\in "
"\\{0, 1\\}$ become Ising spins $s_i = 2x_i - 1$, turning the quadratic "
"energy into an Ising Hamiltonian:"

